1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:04,919
I went to Gazab in New York City's Lower East Side and I was blown away by their modern Indian food.

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:10,580
I started with the chicken wings, which are tossed in their spicy chili tomato sauce, sprinkled with cashew dust,

3
00:00:10,919 --> 00:00:13,640
topped with dried curry leaf, and served with a curry leaf ranch.

4
00:00:14,099 --> 00:00:17,239
Another appetizer you need to get is their patayala chicken tikka.

5
00:00:17,699 --> 00:00:21,980
Chicken thighs covered in their tikka sauce and baked in their tandoor until they look like this.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,260
They're drizzled with butter, some Indian spices, lemon, and they don't let any of that juice go to waste.

7
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:34,359
Served with a chili sour cream and oh my god, possibly the most tender chicken I've ever devoured.

8
00:00:34,719 --> 00:00:40,579
And for my entree, I went with their Parsi Lamb Saliboti, boneless lamb, and a spicy tangy tomato gravy,

9
00:00:40,759 --> 00:00:46,159
which gets simmered with spices, cilantro, and lemon, topped with more cilantro, fried potato sticks,

10
00:00:46,399 --> 00:00:47,640
and drizzled with their red chili.

11
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:50,100
It's served with some fresh made naan,

12
00:00:50,219 --> 00:00:54,460
which gets baked in their tandoor until it's nice and crispy and buttery like this.

13
00:00:55,539 --> 00:00:58,359
This restaurant needs to be on your New York City devout.

